  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting the Registration of Ukrainian Nationals Entering Ireland</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will provide technical support to the register Ukrainian nationals and their family members and issue them with a special &#x201C;temporary protection&#x201D; residence card. This project aims to facilitate safe, orderly and regular migration of Ukrainian nationals arriving in Ireland by the establishment of Registration Processing Center. Through this centre, the provision of in-person related assistance will benefit all Ukrainian national and their family members entering Ireland and seeking for &#x201C;temporary protection&#x201D;. The Department of Justice (DoJ) seek IOM&apos;s expertise for a solution that swiftly facilitates the registration and issuance of temporary protection residence cards to all Ukrainian nationals and their family members arriving in Ireland as of 24 February 2022. This includes inter alia identity verification, assistance to complete registration forms and document completeness checks, scanning of fingerprint and printing of temporary protection residence cards to all applicants. The expertise derived from its longstanding immigration operations serves as the foundation of the support that IOM will provide in Ireland.</narrative>
  </description>
